# Lab Pi sync after changes

When you finish **meaningful edits** to this repository (not trivial typo-only nits), run from the repo root:

```bash
./scripts/sync-to-dev-pi.sh
```

This discovers a unique AryaOS device and mirrors the working tree to
`~/aryaos-sync/`. Set **`ARYAOS_DEV_DEVICE`** when multiple devices are visible
or **`ARYAOS_SSH=pi@<address>`** for an explicit target. The script prefers the
lab private key and supports **`ARYAOS_DEV_DEVICE_PASSWORD`** as a fallback.
Details: [docs/dev-pi.md](docs/dev-pi.md).

If the user only changed portal/CGI/lighttpd pieces and wants them live
immediately, also run `./scripts/sync-portal-review.sh` after the tree sync.

If `sync-to-dev-pi.sh` fails (no network, missing key/password, auth errors), report the error and stop; do not claim the Pi was updated.
